  (jolt-invoke4 (var-deref "clojure.core" "attach-core-doc-meta!") "clojure.core" "every-pred" "Takes a set of predicates and returns a function f that returns true if all of its\n  composing predicates return a logical true value against all of its arguments, else it returns\n  false. Note that f is short-circuiting in that it will stop execution on the first\n  argument that triggers a logical false result against the original predicates." (jolt-list (jolt-vector (jolt-symbol #f "p")) (jolt-vector (jolt-symbol #f "p1") (jolt-symbol #f "p2")) (jolt-vector (jolt-symbol #f "p1") (jolt-symbol #f "p2") (jolt-symbol #f "p3")) (jolt-vector (jolt-symbol #f "p1") (jolt-symbol #f "p2") (jolt-symbol #f "p3") (jolt-symbol #f "&") (jolt-symbol #f "ps")))))
